(ESCC) treated by radiochemotherapy</article-title><source>Am Soc Clin Oncol</source><year>2006</year>Gastrointestinal cancers symposium, third Annual Meeting, San Francisco (abstract no. 45)</citation></ref><ref id="bib6"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Mimura</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name><name><surname>Kono</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name><name><surname>Hanawa</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Mitsui</surname><given-names>F</given-names></name><name><surname>Sugai</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name><name><surname>Miyagawa</surname><given-names>N</given-names></name><name><surname>Ooi</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Fujii</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>frequencies of Her-2&#x0002f;neu expression and gene amplification in patients with oesophageal squamous cell carcinoma</article-title><source>Br J Cancer</source><year>2005b</year><volume>92</volume><fpage>1253</fpage><lpage>1260</lpage><!--PubMed citation query: 'Br J Cancer||92|1253||bib6|'--><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15785739</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib7"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Mimura</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name><name><surname>Kono</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name><name><surname>hanawa</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Kanzaki</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Nakao</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Ooi</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Fujii</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Trastuzumab-mediated antibody-dependent cellular cytotoxicity against esophageal squamous cell carcinoma</article-title><source>Clin Cancer Res</source><year>2005a</year><volume>11</volume><fpage>4898</fpage><lpage>